# Copy to qemu/local.env (gitignored) on a machine where auto-detection in
# qemu/common.sh picks the wrong thing. Plain bash, sourced by the qemu scripts;
# environment variables still override it.

# Rust-enabled kernel build dir (scripts/build_kernel.sh, docs/setup.md).
#KERNEL=$HOME/WS/linux_ktvmx

# Raw ext4 root disk with sshd and root key login (syzkaller create-image.sh style).
#DISK=$HOME/WS/stretch-image/bookworm.img
#DISK=/data/debian-img/trixie.img

# Defaults to $DISK with .img replaced by .id_rsa.
#SSH_KEY=

# Pick another port if 10021 is taken (e.g. a second VM on the same machine).
#PORT=10021
#MEM=2G

# Extra guest kernel command line, for disk images whose boot stalls before sshd
# (boot_vm then says "guest ssh did not come up"; read qemu.log):
#  - "You are in emergency mode" after "FAILED ... Failed to mount /mnt": the image's
#    /etc/fstab mounts something these scripts do not provide (bookworm.img: a virtiofs
#    share, tag myfs, from ~/WS/start_qemu.sh). Mask the mount unit, named after the
#    path (/mnt -> mnt.mount), instead of editing a shared image.
#  - "A start job is running for Raise network interfaces" for minutes: / stayed
#    read-only (no "Remount Root and Kernel File Systems" in the log), dhclient-script
#    cannot write its lease and DECLINEs every offer. `rw` mounts / writable from the
#    start; harmless because the disk is opened with -snapshot.
#APPEND_EXTRA="rw systemd.mask=mnt.mount"
